 "response": "Stedamu's budget is now **$2503K**, which is the result of applying every Finance Office update that has not been withdrawn.\n\n**How the records were applied**\n\n1. **Source filter.** Only Finance Office entries change the budget. Messages from Engineering, Vendor, PMO, Sales, Legal, Marketing, Operations and Facilities were ignored. So were Finance Office notes that do not touch the budget, such as reminders, audits and archived invoices.\n\n2. **Withdrawal chains.** Each chain was worked back from the last withdrawal, which nothing withdraws, so it stands. Each step back flips the status of the record it targets. Examples:\n   - **Update #0002 (\u2212$36K) applies.** #0632 withdrew #0439, which had withdrawn #0112. #0112 withdrew #0078, which had withdrawn #0007. #0007 withdrew #0003, which had withdrawn #0002.\n   - **Update #0010 (\u2212$407K) does not apply.** #1367 withdrew #0845. That reinstates #0175, which cancels #0057. With #0057 gone, #0013 stands and keeps #0010 withdrawn.\n   - **Update #1423 (\u2212$206K) applies.** #1544 withdrew #1522, and #1522 was the withdrawal of #1423.\n\n3. **Running total.** Starting from #0001 (set to $1880K), every remaining change was applied in order. The total passes through:\n\n| After record | Budget |\n|---|---|\n| #0006 | $1282K |\n| #0126 | $4482K |\n| #0448 | $895K |\n| #1111 | $3059K |\n| #1431 | $918K |\n| #1598 (final) | $2503K |\n\nANSWER: $2503K",
